# AI Workflow Router

Use project skills instead of long ad hoc prompts.

## Skill routing

Use `.claude/skills/grill-with-docs/SKILL.md` when the user wants to stress-test a plan, architecture, domain model, product concept, or implementation approach.

Use `.claude/skills/handoff/SKILL.md` when the user wants a compact summary, restart-safe continuation doc, or handoff for another session.

Use `.claude/skills/caveman/SKILL.md` when the user wants compressed technical communication or explicitly asks for brief / caveman style.

## Token discipline

- Do not load skill files unless relevant.
- Do not paste whole docs into chat.
- Prefer referencing paths over duplicating content.
- Keep default responses concise.
- For long tasks, inspect relevant project files first, then answer.